# Bash prompt, option 2 ("don't ask again for: <prefix> *"): a second,
# EXACTLY identical command runs without a prompt.
#
# Read from source rather than the rendered label: the option's label
# text promises a prefix rule ("npm test *"), but the session grant
# (internal/claude/permission/permission.go's key()/grantSession) is
# keyed on toolName + "::" + the exact primaryArg string, not a glob — a
# *different* command sharing the same first two words would still
# prompt again. This scenario repeats the identical command deliberately
# (matching the task brief's "a second identical command"), and the
# EXPECT below records the label/mechanism gap as a discrepancy rather
# than silently assuming the friendlier, prefix-matching behaviour the
# label describes.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/permissions-bash-option2.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE run the upload tests twice
KEY enter
WAITFOR /approval needed/ 20
SHOT first-prompt
EXPECT /npm test -- upload/
EXPECT /Yes, and don.t ask again for: npm test \*/
KEY 2
WAITFOR /Both test runs done/ 20
SHOT second-command-no-prompt
EXPECT_NOT /approval needed/
EXPECT /second one didn.t need approval/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
